Comments: [Evaluator: Christian Iliadis; Date: 04/05/2024]
1.  Er > 500 keV: from Tab. 34.20 in Endt 1990; resonance energies were computed from the compiled excitation energies; resonance strengths were normalized relative
    to our adopted strength of the Elab = 1211 keV resonance in 34S(p,g)35Cl.
2.  Er = 434 and 493 keV: weighted average of directly measured strengths of Waanders et al. 1983 (renormalized) and Fallis et al. 2013; resonance energies were 
    computed from Ex values in Parikh et al. 2014.
3.  Lower-lying resonances: energies from Parikh et al. 2014; strengths either from C2S measured by Parikh et al. 2014 or directly measured by Fallis et al. 2013.
4.  Er = 294 and 312 keV: adopted directly measured strengths of Fallis et al. 2013.
5.  Direct capture: estimated using experimental C2S values from Endt 1977, Endt & can der Leun 1978, Parikh et al. 2014.
